## Package-Time First-Party Actionability Recheck and Gold-Artifact Spawn Gate

Operational reference: `BLUEPRINT.md` §141.13-§141.15
(`CAREER_OS_PACKAGE_GATE_HARDENING_V1`) and
`docs/resume/BORA_PACKAGE_SPAWN_GATE_V1.json` lock the correction earned
by three reproduced live defects: a Santander package produced before the
exact first-party requisition was proven actionable; a DraftKings resume
that drifted from the canonical gold family and leaked internal-system
language; and Point32Health Business Analyst R9102, where an HTTP-200 dead
page retained the requisition token and the operator incorrectly continued
despite `TITLE_MATCH=False`. This section operationally enforces §141.13-§141.15;
not restated here in full.

**Package-time recheck.** Immediately before Claude drafting, DOCX
mutation, cover-letter drafting, or any other meaningful package work,
re-open the exact current first-party employer requisition in the
current operating session and re-establish the full positive semantic
quorum: matching role/title identity, matching requisition identity,
substantive current job-description content, and a current actionable
application route. This route/instruction element requires repeating
`BLUEPRINT.md` §135.1's (`END_USER_APPLICATION_TRANSITION_QUORUM_V1`)
end-user application transition validation: the package-time recheck
must repeat both elements of §135.1 again, fresh, in the current operating
session -- (1) exact job-detail validation (the exact public job-detail
URL still establishes the current exact role) and (2) the application
transition exercised or otherwise directly resolved to the actual
current end-user application destination. Prior pursuit-time success on
either element alone is insufficient at package time; both must be
repeated. HTTP 200,
a requisition token, ATS shell, Apply-like control, or ATS API/index/
search metadata alone never satisfies this gate; explicit dead/error-page
text, a generic careers/search redirect, loss of exact role/requisition
identity, or an unusable application transition (including a
login/paywall dead end with no recoverable application path) fails closed even when
HTTP 200 or the requisition token is present.
**Auth carve-out (not a veto):** a role-preserving login/SSO step that
continues into a usable, exact-role destination -- identity preserved
and a recoverable application path beyond it -- is not itself a veto;
only an auth dead end with no recoverable path, or identity loss across
it, fails closed. An Apply control, ATS API/index/metadata, HTTP 200, or
a requisition token cannot substitute for that resolution. This does not blacklist
Workday or any ATS vendor. This is §135's existing
successfully-established test, applied again at package time. A prior
pursuit-time pass does not by itself
satisfy this recheck. A blank/contentless shell, a JavaScript-only page
with no recoverable JD content, a generic careers/search redirect, a
page-not-found response, an expired/closed page, an identity mismatch,
or a missing current application route fails the gate; discovery
indexes, aggregators, cached snippets, prior captures, chat summaries,
and memory cannot rescue it. On failure, generate or revise no package
for that role; preserve historical analysis if useful; report the role
as non-actionable/verification-required using the existing
`role_status`/`source_verification_status` axes (`schemas/job.schema.json`)
— never a new enum.

**Gold-artifact spawn gate.** Resume spawning must clone the exact
current Bora gold-quality DOCX artifact (§141.10,
`docs/resume/BORA_GOLD_QUALITY_REFERENCE_V1.json`) as the starting
document when available, with its SHA-256 verified against that record
before making bounded content edits. Do not reconstruct the gold family
from scratch with a fresh document/template, ad-hoc tables, margins,
typography, or section grammar merely by reading doctrine. If the exact
artifact is unavailable or its hash does not match, stop with
`GOLD_REFERENCE_ARTIFACT_REQUIRED` rather than improvising a new
template.

**Internal-jargon translation.** Candidate-facing package text must not
expose internal Career OS/governance/evidence-system/implementation-
control language (e.g. human approval, operating system, fail-closed,
queue-level eligibility, deterministic boundary, Candidate Truth) unless
the exact term is independently job-relevant and recruiter-natural;
otherwise translate into ordinary professional American English. This
extends the Candidate-Facing Style section above and §141.11's
human-naturalness QA dimension.

**Pre-delivery reject conditions.** Before delivery to Bora, package QA
must explicitly reject a PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY heading, noncanonical
section order, noncanonical Title | Employer work grammar, missing
required gold-family hyperlink objects, rendered overflow/clipping/
overlap, sub-92-percent meaningful utilization, or other material
gold-family structural drift, unless an explicit employer format
instruction requires a documented exception.

This is a doctrine/operating-gate lock only — no generator, renderer, or
automated validator is authorized by this section (§133/§134 Non-Goals
continue to govern).

