survivor packages and a hash-verified cover-letter gold reference.

**Four-artifact completeness.** Every genuine survivor role's FINAL
package must durably contain résumé DOCX, résumé PDF, cover-letter DOCX,
and cover-letter PDF, unless Bora explicitly opts out of the cover
letter for that specific application. §140.1's DOCX-first submission
default and §140.9's durable-completeness rule govern which single
format is actually submitted versus which artifacts must exist in the
FINAL package — an employer format instruction controls submission
choice only, never durable package generation.

**Cover-letter gold-artifact clone requirement.** Cover-letter DOCX
construction must clone the exact hash-verified
`Bora_Chaush_Cover_Letter_Gold_Reference.docx` (SHA-256
`264f7a8cc194e0211ce7f0af411b0ab6c07fa2438c557aa2e470536fded67e90`)
rather than reconstructing a template from doctrine text, mirroring the
resume gold-artifact spawn gate (§141.14). The gold DOCX's existence
and SHA-256 match alone control clone authority and spawn permission:
if the exact gold DOCX artifact is unavailable or its SHA-256 does not
match, stop with `COVER_LETTER_GOLD_REFERENCE_ARTIFACT_REQUIRED`. A
rendered visual-reference PDF of that same gold DOCX is separately
recorded (SHA-256
`0b7da43108b0fae5ba4211078b4308cad9014d1e11cb533bc25ed64feec8df42`) and
must be verified whenever that PDF is actually used for
visual-fidelity QA — but a missing or mismatched visual-reference PDF
hash alone does not trigger this stop condition. This gold reference is
presentation/quality/template authority only — never Candidate Truth.
Role-specific cover-letter content must remain grounded exclusively in
the verified current JD, Match Truth (§140.4 crosswalk), and approved
Candidate Truth/evidence. Bora's approved Northeastern University
R141882 cover-letter family is the motivating exemplar for this lock;
its own role-specific facts must never be copied into universal doctrine
or another role's cover letter.

**Cover-letter content and style.** One U.S. Letter page;
recruiter-natural American business English (Candidate-Facing Style,
